  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender, HIV and AIDS in the context of poverty alleviation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project goal: Transformed institutions and men regarding gender justice issues in the context of HIV and AIDS and poverty in the Zululand.

Outcomes 
1. Capacitated leadership in the Zululand on gender, poverty and HIV and AIDS issues  
2. Community in the Zululand actively involved in the advocacy  and lobbying 
3. Functional Poverty alleviation initiatives that minimize the effects of HIV and AIDS to women and children
4. Gender based violence victims and PLWAs are able to take charge of their own lives.
The KwaZulu Regional Christian Council (KRCC), churches and communities in the province propose to implement a 3 year programme titled &#x2018;&#x2018;Gender, HIV and AIDS in the context of poverty alleviation&#x2019;&#x2019;. The goal of the project is to transform attitudes and perceptions, gender stereotyping of women and HIV and AIDS, poverty in Zululand of KZN. This will be done through a two pronged approach i.e. (i) creating space for local churches to engage in activities aimed at political and socio-economic transformation in relation to poverty, gender discrimination and HIV and AIDS within the communities they serve and (ii) providing psychosocial support to women and children who have been abused as well as those who live with HIV and AIDS. This programme will be implemented in rural areas, providing a unique opportunity for partners, civil society to contribute positively to areas that are normally shunned.</narrative>
  </description>
